---
/** Editable maintained BASIC with the accepted lesson/modal interaction. */
import BasicListing from './BasicListing.astro';
import '../styles/basic-machine.css';
interface Props {src:string;name:string;keypad?:boolean}
const {src,name,keypad=false}=Astro.props;
---
<section class="basic-playground" data-name={name}>
<BasicListing src={src} name={name}/>
<button class="return-spectrum" type="button" hidden>Return to your Spectrum</button>
<dialog class="lesson-machine" aria-labelledby={`machine-${name}`}><header class="machine-heading"><div><h2 id={`machine-${name}`}>Your Spectrum</h2><p>48K · PAL</p></div><button class="return-reading" type="button">Close and return</button></header><p class="session-guide">Click the screen to send it keys. Tab returns to the controls.</p><div class="live-machine"><canvas width="352" height="296" tabindex="0" aria-label="ZX Spectrum screen. Click to type; Tab returns to page controls."></canvas></div>
<div class="machine-controls"><button class="pause-machine" type="button" disabled>Pause</button><button class="restart-machine" type="button" disabled>Restart Spectrum</button><label><input type="checkbox" class="machine-sound"/> Sound</label></div><p class="machine-status" role="status">Not started.</p><details class="machine-failure" hidden><summary>Startup error details</summary><pre></pre></details><button class="edit-basic" type="button">Back to the listing</button>
<details class="machine-input" open={keypad}><summary>On-screen keys</summary><fieldset class="machine-input-keys" disabled aria-label="Spectrum input keys"><button type="button" data-key="Digit1">1</button><button type="button" data-key="Digit2">2</button><button type="button" data-key="Digit3">3</button><button type="button" data-key="Digit4">4</button><button type="button" data-key="Digit5">5</button><button type="button" data-key="Digit6">6</button><button type="button" data-key="Digit7">7</button><button type="button" data-key="Digit8">8</button><button type="button" data-key="Digit9">9</button><button type="button" data-key="Digit0">0</button><button type="button" data-key="Backspace">Delete</button><button type="button" data-key="Enter">Enter</button><button type="button" data-key="Escape">BREAK</button><button type="button" data-key="KeyQ">Q · quit</button></fieldset></details><details class="machine-help"><summary>Keyboard and Session</summary><p>Shift is CAPS SHIFT. Alt or Option is SYMBOL SHIFT. Comma and full stop use their Spectrum key combinations automatically. Escape sends BREAK while the screen has focus. Enter submits a line. Restart clears this session. Returning to the lesson pauses it.</p><p>To type into this screen, use a physical keyboard. On a touchscreen, edit the listing in the lesson and choose Run this code. Open On-screen keys here to answer numeric INPUT prompts or send BREAK.</p><p>Runs the Sinclair 48K ROM. Amstrad have kindly given their permission for the redistribution of their copyrighted material but retain that copyright.</p><a href="https://emu198x.github.io/downloads/">Download Emu198x for desktop</a></details>
<details class="machine-transcript"><summary>Screen text</summary><pre aria-live="off">The Spectrum has not started yet.</pre></details>
<p class="paused-note" hidden>Your Spectrum is paused. Resume to continue where you left it.</p></dialog>

</section>
<script src="../lib/basic-machine.ts"></script>
